            "engineering-quality": {
              "availability": "available",
              "findings": [
                {
                  "evidence": "template/scripts/finish_task.py:954-971 (new helper) and :1060-1082 (original block). Both call queue_local_status, then sync_merged_task with the same SystemExit messages. The existing test had to change its side_effect from [None, waiting] to [None, None, waiting] to cope with the extra read.",
                  "id": "duplicated-merged-queue-sync",
                  "severity": "advisory",
                  "summary": "The new sync_queue_merged_task helper copies the existing queue-observation and merged-sync block further down in main(). Finish now reads the queue PR state twice and calls sync_merged_task twice on the merged path. The second call is idempotent, but it costs an extra PR read and leaves two copies "
                },
                {
                  "evidence": "template/scripts/finish_task.py:1049 calls sync_queue_merged_task before managed_candidate(work). The orphan and provenance checks follow at :1053-1054. The added tests cover only candidate=True.",
                  "id": "merged-sync-ahead-of-orphan-check",
                  "severity": "advisory",
                  "summary": "The early sync now runs for every coordinator-mode PR finish, not only for managed candidates. It fast-forwards the worktree before require_no_orphan_active_openspec and require_delivery_provenance run. A merged non-candidate task is therefore synchronized before the gates that previously preceded i"
                }
              ],
              "perspective": "engineering-quality",
              "report_sha256": "edc4e2ea4fdbd7f0e5d360ea26111e2b449673789bbc2197562df2db28d33d8e"
            },
            "spec-fidelity": {
              "availability": "available",
              "findings": [
                {
                  "evidence": "template/scripts/finish_task.py:1049 calls sync_queue_merged_task. Lines 1060-1082 run queue_local_status and sync_merged_task again for the same merged state. The updated test side_effect=[waiting, waiting] / [None, None, waiting] shows the doubled read.",
                  "id": "merged-sync-repeated-downstream",
                  "severity": "advisory",
                  "summary": "The merged queue state is observed and synchronized twice per finish. The new early helper and the existing queue block both call local_status and sync_merged_task. The design says only 'one extra PR read' and does not describe the second synchronization. It also leaves duplicate logic and error mes"
                },
                {
                  "evidence": "sync_queue_merged_task returns False when `not queue_enabled(work)`. The new spec says 'When the exact PR of the task branch is merged, finish SHALL run the post-merge reconcile path ... An unreadable PR state SHALL stop finish explicitly.' The proposal Impact lists '`lifecycle_preflight` board condition'. The diff leaves the preflight code unchanged.",
                  "id": "merged-detection-queue-only",
                  "severity": "advisory",
                  "summary": "The spec requires reconcile ahead of handoff whenever the exact PR of the task branch is merged. The implementation detects this only through publication_queue.enabled and local_status. The proposal also lists a lifecycle_preflight board-condition change in its Impact section, but the diff has no su"
                }
              ],
              "perspective": "spec-fidelity",
              "report_sha256": "5c6d645569f445f7d9aa5d28019e5c6e20eaa4c3ad2e96242e34181a379f69be"
            }
